-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Dify
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ChatDify generates workflow DSL for Dify (https://github.com/langgenius/dify)
and can optionally use Dify's own node entity definitions for static
validation. Dify source code is NOT redistributed as part of the ChatDify
package. When static validation is enabled, ChatDify imports Dify from a
source tree that the user obtains separately (via the `dify` git submodule,
`chatdify dify fetch`, or `--dify-src`).

Dify is licensed under the Dify Open Source License, a modified Apache
License 2.0 with additional conditions. See
https://github.com/langgenius/dify/blob/main/LICENSE for details.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Knowledge base
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`chatdify/kg/` contains Dify node references and workflow templates. Some
templates were adapted from publicly shared Dify workflows; credentials and
organization-specific information have been removed. If you are the author
of a template and would like it attributed differently or removed, please
open an issue.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Benchmark input files (test_cases/chatdify/data/)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Unless listed below, the input files are synthetic and all names, companies,
identifiers and numbers in them are fictional.

- online_retail.csv, online_retail_sample_500.csv: derived from the "Online
  Retail" dataset by Daqing Chen, UCI Machine Learning Repository
  (https://doi.org/10.24432/C5BW33), licensed under CC BY 4.0. Dates were
  shifted and rows sampled.
- orders.csv, brands.csv: from the BikeStores sample database
  (https://www.sqlservertutorial.net/getting-started/sql-server-sample-database/).
- stock.xlsx: public daily quotes of the SSE Composite Index.
- deepseek-r1.pdf: "DeepSeek-R1: Incentivizing Reasoning Capability in LLMs
  via Reinforcement Learning", DeepSeek-AI, arXiv:2501.12948. Copyright
  remains with the authors; included only as a test document.
